{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917314694},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me break down what I need to do:\n\n1. I have two data sources:\n   - Farmers markets data: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\n   - Census/population data: https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\n\n2. I need to:\n   - Calculate total farmers markets from the first dataset\n   - Get total U.S. residents from the census file\n   - Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n   - Provide the answer to 4 decimal places\n   - One confident sentence only\n   - Use tools to do the math (never do math in my head or manually)\n   - Verify everything with xorq_verify\n\n3. According to the project instructions, I should:\n   - First check if there are semantic models that cover this\n   - Run xorq_semantic_models and xorq_catalog_list_aliases\n   - If needed, ingest the sources as catalog aliases\n   - Use xorq_select to get the actual values\n   - Use xorq_verify to verify my answer\n\nLet me start by orienting: check for semantic models and existing aliases, then ingest the data if needed.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking the xorq catalog for any existing data and then ingest the sources if needed."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01YJpRGDudR